-- title:
--   Sum of local invariants is unchanged by corestriction
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ and $F$ be number fields with $F/E$ finite Galois, and write $G = F \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[E]} F$ for its Galois group and $\mathbb{A}_F =$ `AdeleRing (𝓞 F) F`. The Galois descent datum is an `IdeleGaloisDescent (𝓞 F) E F`, i.e. a monoid homomorphism $g \mapsto D.\mathrm{act}\,g$ from $G$ to the ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_F$, each of which is continuous, and which is compatible with the structure map in the sense that $D.\mathrm{act}\,g$ applied to the image of $x \in F$ is the image of $g x$. The group $G$ is assumed to act multiplicatively and distributively on $\mathbb{A}_F^{\times}$, and the hypothesis `hactI` says that this action agrees with the one obtained from $D$ by applying the units functor, namely `D.unitsAct`. Throughout, $\mathbb{A}_F^{\times}$ is viewed, written additively, as a $\mathbb{Z}$-linear representation of $G$ via `Rep.ofMulDistribMulAction`, and likewise for the unit groups of local completions with their decomposition groups; for a finite place $w$ of $F$ (a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_F$), [`NumberField.PlaceDecomp.decomp E F w`](def/NumberField_PlaceDecompositionAction.html#L82) denotes the decomposition subgroup of $G$ at $w$ (the decomposition subgroup of the valuation subring of $w$), and [`NumberField.PlaceAbove.above`](def/NumberField_PlaceAbove.html#L27) denotes the chosen finite place of $F$ above a given finite place of the base.
--
--   The data are: a subgroup $H \le G$; a transversal $\tau$ for $H$ in the sense of [`groupCohomology.Cores.Transversal`](def/GroupCohomology_Corestriction2.html#L13), that is a section $\sigma : G/H \to G$ of the projection with $\sigma(1) = 1$; and a class $y \in H^2(H, \mathbb{A}_F^{\times})$, the second group cohomology of the restriction of the above representation along the inclusion $H \hookrightarrow G$.
--
--   Local projections at the full decomposition groups: a family `prG` assigning to each finite place $w$ of $F$ a morphism of representations of $\mathrm{decomp}\,E\,F\,w$ from the restriction of $\mathbb{A}_F^{\times}$ to that subgroup into the units of the $w$-adic completion $F_w$, together with the hypothesis that `prG w` carries the additive copy of an idèle unit $x$ to the additive copy of its $w$-component `finPart w x` (the $w$-evaluation of the finite part of $x$).
--
--   Local data at the finite places of $E$ (a group of hypotheses, summarised here): for each finite place $v$ of $E$, with $w(v) =$ `above E F v` and $D_{w(v)} = \mathrm{decomp}\,E\,F\,w(v)$, a prime $q_v$, a subfield $L'_v$ of a fixed algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}_{q_v}$ which is finite over $\mathbb{Q}_{q_v}$, a multiplicative semiring action of $D_{w(v)}$ on $L'_v$ and a compatible distributive action on $(L'_v)^{\times}$, and a ring isomorphism $\Phi_v : F_{w(v)} \xrightarrow{\sim} L'_v$; the accompanying compatibility hypotheses state that $D_{w(v)}$ fixes the image of $\mathbb{Q}_{q_v}$ in $L'_v$, that the action on units is compatible with the inclusion of units into $L'_v$, and that $\Phi_v$ is $D_{w(v)}$-equivariant. Further, a subfield $K_{0,v}$ of the same algebraic closure, finite over $\mathbb{Q}_{q_v}$, which is a base for $L'_v$ in the sense of [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.IsBase`](def/ExtCitation_LocalLevel_FundamentalClass.html#L13): $K_{0,v} \le L'_v$ and an element of $L'_v$ lies in $K_{0,v}$ exactly when it is fixed by every element of $D_{w(v)}$. Finally, a morphism $\theta_v$ of $D_{w(v)}$-representations from $(L'_v)^{\times}$ to $F_{w(v)}^{\times}$ realising $\Phi_v^{-1}$ on underlying elements, and a class $u'_v \in H^2(D_{w(v)}, (L'_v)^{\times})$ satisfying [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.IsLocalFundamentalClass`](def/ExtCitation_LocalLevel_FundamentalClass.html#L60); the latter predicate (summarised here) requires that for every finite extension $M$ of $\mathbb{Q}_{q_v}$ inside the algebraic closure with $L'_v \le M$, every finite group $\tilde H$ acting faithfully and semiring-compatibly on $M$ with distributive action on $M^{\times}$, all normal subgroups $N_L, N_n \le \tilde H$, every isomorphism $e : D_{w(v)} \simeq \tilde H / N_L$, every $\varphi \in \tilde H$ and unit $\pi$ of $M$ forming an unramified-overlayer datum (fixed base $\mathbb{Q}_{q_v}$-scalars, $K_{0,v}$ and $L'_v$ cut out as the fixed fields of $\tilde H$ and of $N_L$, compatibility of the two actions through $e$, $\tilde H/N_n$ of the same order as $D_{w(v)}$ and generated by the image of $\varphi$, the Frobenius congruence for $\varphi$ on the $N_n$-fixed integral elements, and $\pi$ an $\tilde H$-fixed uniformiser of $K_{0,v}$ dominating all $N_n$-fixed elements of norm $< 1$), and every comparison morphism $\iota$ inducing the inclusion on units, the image of $u'_v$ under the map on $H^2$ induced by $e^{-1}$ and $\iota$ equals the inflation of the class of the explicit "carry" $2$-cocycle attached to $\pi$ and the cyclic generator.
--
--   The local reading of the corestriction: an integer-valued function $n$ on the finite places of $E$ together with the hypothesis that for every such $v$, the image of [`groupCohomology.Cores.cores`](def/GroupCohomology_Corestriction2.html#L178) of $y$ along $\tau$ under the map on $H^2$ induced by the inclusion $D_{w(v)} \hookrightarrow G$ and by `prG w(v)` equals $n_v$ times the image of $u'_v$ under the map induced by the identity of $D_{w(v)}$ and $\theta_v$.
--
--   Local projections at the intersections with $H$: a family `prH` assigning to each finite place $w$ of $F$ a morphism of representations of $H \cap \mathrm{decomp}\,E\,F\,w$ from the restriction of $\mathbb{A}_F^{\times}$ (restricted first to $H$, then along $H \cap \mathrm{decomp}\,E\,F\,w \le H$) to the restriction of $F_w^{\times}$ along $H \cap \mathrm{decomp}\,E\,F\,w \le \mathrm{decomp}\,E\,F\,w$, again with the hypothesis that `prH w` sends the additive copy of an idèle unit $x$ to the additive copy of `finPart w x`.
--
--   Local data at the finite places of the fixed field $F^H =$ `IntermediateField.fixedField H` (the same group of hypotheses as above, with the same summary): for each finite place $v$ of $F^H$, with $w(v) =$ `above F^H F v`, primes $q_{H,v}$, finite extensions $L_{H,v}$ of $\mathbb{Q}_{q_{H,v}}$ with actions of $\mathrm{decomp}\,E\,F\,w(v)$ on $L_{H,v}$ and on its units, ring isomorphisms $\Phi_{H,v} : F_{w(v)} \xrightarrow{\sim} L_{H,v}$ with the three compatibility conditions, bases $K_{H,v}$ finite over $\mathbb{Q}_{q_{H,v}}$ satisfying `IsBase` for $L_{H,v}$ and $\mathrm{decomp}\,E\,F\,w(v)$, morphisms $\theta_{H,v}$ realising $\Phi_{H,v}^{-1}$, and classes $u_{H,v} \in H^2(\mathrm{decomp}\,E\,F\,w(v), L_{H,v}^{\times})$ satisfying `IsLocalFundamentalClass`. Note that here the groups are the full decomposition groups of $w(v)$ in $G$, not their intersections with $H$.
--
--   The local reading of $y$ itself: an integer-valued function $m$ on the finite places of $F^H$ together with the hypothesis that for every such $v$, the image of $y$ under the map on $H^2$ induced by the inclusion $H \cap \mathrm{decomp}\,E\,F\,w(v) \le H$ and by `prH w(v)` equals $m_v$ times the image, under the map induced by the inclusion $H \cap \mathrm{decomp}\,E\,F\,w(v) \le \mathrm{decomp}\,E\,F\,w(v)$ and the identity morphism of the restricted representation, of the image of $u_{H,v}$ under the map induced by the identity of $\mathrm{decomp}\,E\,F\,w(v)$ and $\theta_{H,v}$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is the single equality in $\mathbb{Q}/\mathbb{Z} =$ `AddCircle (1 : ℚ)` of two `finsum`s,
--   $$\sum_{v}^{\mathrm{f}} \Big[\frac{n_v}{\#\,\mathrm{decomp}\,E\,F\,(\text{above } E\,F\,v)}\Big] \;=\; \sum_{v'}^{\mathrm{f}} \Big[\frac{m_{v'}}{\#\,\big(H \cap \mathrm{decomp}\,E\,F\,(\text{above } F^H\,F\,v')\big)}\Big],$$
--   the first sum taken over all finite places $v$ of $E$ and the second over all finite places $v'$ of $F^H$, where the rational numbers $n_v/\#D_{w(v)}$ and $m_{v'}/\#(H \cap D_{w(v')})$ are taken modulo $1$.
--
--   This is the compatibility of the global invariant map with the transfer: the sum of the local invariants of the corestriction of an idèle class from $H$ to $G$, read off at the chosen places above the finite places of $E$, agrees modulo $1$ with the sum of the local invariants of the class itself, read off at the chosen places above the finite places of the fixed field $F^H$. It is used in the construction of invariant idèle classes with prescribed local behaviour, which is where the two statements citing it, on classes under a $p$-group hypothesis, draw on it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_M4aHerbrand_finsum_div_natCard_decomp_cores_eq_finsum_div_natCard_inf_decomp.lean

